From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:28:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: iPad 5 (J71t): Enable the GPU
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The powervr driver takes the A9's GPU node now and starts its firmware.
Enabled on the J71t, the board Berkay Kösebay's driver runs this GPU on
and the one whose firmware recipe has the GPU's image. The J72t and the
S8003 phones keep it disabled until theirs have it: without the file the
driver would only fail to load it at every boot.

The driver binds only with powervr.exp_hw_support=1 as long as the GPU
does not render.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts
index 733cefc..4775055 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts
@@ -24,3 +24,10 @@
 &wifi {
 	brcm,board-type = "apple,feara";
 };
+
+/*
+ * The GPU: the powervr driver starts its firmware. It does not render yet.
+ */
+&gpu {
+	status = "okay";
+};
